Desktop detach/reattach: three root causes found by reading vendored sources, each masked by the previous one.

1. DETACH NO-OP: 54ec328's diagnosis (remote content -> no IPC) was right that a remote grant was needed, but wrong in mechanism: __TAURI_INTERNALS__ IS injected unconditionally (tauri-2.10.3 manager/webview.rs:160, main_frame_script list) — gating is per-IPC-call, not at injection. So the Tauri branch always runs on desktop, and getByLabel() dies first: it calls plugin:window|get_all_windows (webviewWindow.js:25), never granted. Fix: core:window:allow-get-all-windows in remote-webview.json. Also verified two dead ends: RemoteUrlPattern wildcards empty pathnames (tauri-utils acl/mod.rs:285), so "http://localhost:8935" matches all paths; and the URL is Remote per is_local_url (not relative to devUrl/frontendDist).

2. REATTACH WHITE WINDOW: first tried JS window.close() in the detached page (wry maps it to DestroyWindow). WRONG on desktop: the hwnd wry destroys is its WRY_WEBVIEW container child-HWND (wry-0.54.3 webview2/mod.rs:615 + create_container_hwnd; tauri uses WebviewKind::WindowContent -> build() -> new_in_hwnd), NOT the native window. Result: live blank window + stale android-live label; getByLabel then returns a dead handle and setFocus throws forever. Fix: getCurrentWindow().close() (plugin:window|close) from the detached page; capability now applies to windows ["main","android-live"] and grants core:window:allow-close. Deliberately NO window.close() fallback on desktop — that IS the white-screen path. Browser keeps window.close() (script-opened popup).

3. CLOSE SWALLOWED BY TRAY: with proper close(), still no reattach and no re-detach — main.rs on_window_event applied hide-to-tray (prevent_close + hide) to EVERY window. Hidden != destroyed: label stays registered, tauri://destroyed never fires, next detach focuses an invisible window. Fix: scope to window.label() == "main".

Reattach signal: main window registers w.once('tauri://destroyed') — WebviewWindow.once uses target {kind:'WebviewWindow', label} and emit_to_window matches Window|WebviewWindow kinds by label (manager/window.rs:137), so cross-window delivery works; needs core:event:allow-listen + allow-unlisten (once() unlistens after firing). Browser: poll popup.closed 1s. Main-reload recovery: onMount re-hooks via getByLabel. detachedDestroyHooked flag prevents listener stacking; listeners are label-keyed so a pre-error listener still catches a later window's destroy.

Bezel resize (separate complaint): the aspect-ratio outline used height:100% + max-width:100%, and percentage heights don't reliably resolve through flex items -> vertical resizes ignored, and when width clamped the explicit height won (distortion). Fix: wrapper is [container-type:size], bezel width: min(100cqw, calc(100cqh * ratio)) with aspect-ratio from deviceW/H — true contain-fit on both axes. cq units are Chromium 105+, fine for WebView2.

Security shape documented in PR-android.md (uncommitted PR body): worst case from frontend XSS with these grants = open/close/focus/enumerate windows; fs/shell/dialog/clipboard remain non-remote. Ports pinned — the XPRESSCLAW_PORT=8936 escape hatch will break detach by design; add the port to remote-webview.json urls if that ever matters.

Also committed gen/schemas/windows-schema.json — its linux/macOS/desktop peers were already tracked; it had sat untracked since the first Windows build.

Runtime-verified by fahreza on the installed app (01:14 build): detach -> reattach button -> rail auto-reopens -> re-detach spawns; native X same; outline tracks both axes.
